t Alaska. In this striking blend of nature writing, whale science, and memoir, Doreen Cunningham interweaves two stories: tracking the extraordinary northward migration of the grey whales with a mischievous toddler in tow and living with an Iñupiaq family in Alaska seven years earlier. Throughout the journey she explores the stories of the whales and their young calves-their history, their habits, and their attempts to survive the changes humans have brought to the ocean. Cunningham's voice is powerful: sharp, profound, sensitive, and unflinching. A story of courage and resilience, Soundings is about the migrating whales and all we can learn from them as they mother, adapt, and endure, their lives interrupted and threatened by global warming.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-soundings-journeys-in-the-company-of-whales-doreen-cunningham.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.509,"accessibilityScore":0.096,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"memoiristic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"memoir\"","catalog text contains \"memoir of\"","memoir/autobiography subject or topic"]},{"id":"narrative","score":0.8,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"story of\"","catalog text contains \"stories of\"","catalog text contains \"journey\"","catalog text contains \"interweaves\""]},{"id":"biographical","score":0.58,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["catalog text contains \"family\"","catalog text contains \"mother\"","biography subject or topic"]},{"id":"character_driven","score":0.3,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"family\"","catalog text contains \"mother\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":18,"criticalRenown":58,"controversy":4,"llmAffinity":82,"affinityResidual":10.32,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.88,"criticalRenown":0.78,"controversy":0.85,"llmAffinity":0.86},"tags":{"craft":"prose-style","evidence":"reportage